@page "/first-component"
@page "/components/getting-started"

<SeoHead CanonicalPath="/first-component" Title="Build your first Quark component | Quark Suite" Description="Create a working Blazor workspace card with a labelled input, generated icon, save action, and status message. Copy the complete Razor example." />

<DocumentationPage Title="Build your first Quark component" Description="Create a working Blazor workspace card with a labelled input, generated icon, save action, and status message. Copy the complete Razor example.">

<Section Id="before-you-begin">
    <H2>Start from the installed app</H2>
    <Paragraph>Complete the <Anchor Href="installation">installation guide</Anchor> first. This example exercises the generated CSS, Lucide provider, value binding, and event handling together.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="try-it">
    <H2>Try it here</H2>
    <Paragraph>Change the workspace name and save. The message updates locally; the example does not send data to a server.</Paragraph>
    <Card Class="max-w-md">
    <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Your first Quark component</CardTitle>
        <CardDescription>Give your workspace a name.</CardDescription>
    </CardHeader>
    <CardContent>
        <Field>
            <FieldLabel For="workspace-name">Workspace name</FieldLabel>
            <Input Id="workspace-name" @bind-Value="_name" />
        </Field>
    </CardContent>
    <CardFooter>
        <Button OnClick="Save">
            <Icon Name="LucideIcon.Check" aria-hidden="true" />
            Save workspace
        </Button>
    </CardFooter>
</Card>
<Paragraph role="status">@_message</Paragraph>


</Section>

<Section Id="copy-the-page">
    <H2>Copy the complete page</H2>
    <Paragraph>Create <Code>Pages/QuarkStart.razor</Code>, paste this code, build the app, and navigate to <Code>/quark-start</Code>:</Paragraph>
    <CodeEditor Text="@first" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
</Section>

<Section Id="what-you-built">
    <H2>What each part does</H2>
    <UnorderedList><UnorderedListItem><Code>CardHeader</Code>, <Code>CardContent</Code>, and <Code>CardFooter</Code> organize the interface into composable parts.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Code>FieldLabel</Code> points to the input's ID, giving the control a meaningful label.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Code>bind-Value</Code> connects the input to a C# field.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Code>LucideIcon.Check</Code> gives the icon generator a source-visible SVG reference.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Code>OnClick</Code> calls the save handler; the status message reflects the updated state.</UnorderedListItem></UnorderedList>
</Section>

<Section Id="make-it-yours">
    <H2>Turn it into an application feature</H2>
    <Paragraph>Replace the local handler with your application service, then add <Anchor Href="components/validation">validation</Anchor> and saving feedback. Use <Anchor Href="properties">typed styling</Anchor> to change the layout or <Anchor Href="themes">theme tokens</Anchor> to apply your brand across components.</Paragraph>
    <Paragraph>Next: <Anchor Href="components/dialog">dialogs</Anchor>, <Anchor Href="components/datatables">data tables</Anchor>, <Anchor Href="components/charts">charts</Anchor>, or the <Anchor Href="components">full component catalog</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

</DocumentationPage>

@code {
    private const string first = @"@page ""/quark-start""
@using Soenneker.Quark
@using Soenneker.Lucide.Enums.Icons

<Card Class=""max-w-md"">
    <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Your first Quark component</CardTitle>
        <CardDescription>Give your workspace a name.</CardDescription>
    </CardHeader>
    <CardContent>
        <Field>
            <FieldLabel For=""workspace-name"">Workspace name</FieldLabel>
            <Input Id=""workspace-name"" @bind-Value=""_name"" />
        </Field>
    </CardContent>
    <CardFooter>
        <Button OnClick=""Save"">
            <Icon Name=""LucideIcon.Check"" aria-hidden=""true"" />
            Save workspace
        </Button>
    </CardFooter>
</Card>
<Paragraph role=""status"">@_message</Paragraph>

@code {
    private string? _name = ""My workspace"";
    private string _message = ""Changes are saved only in this example."";

    private void Save()
    {
        _message = $""Saved: {_name}"";
    }
}";
}

@code {
    private string? _name = "My workspace";
    private string _message = "Changes are saved only in this example.";
    private void Save() => _message = $"Saved: {_name}";
}
